# The blanket *.json above swallows the Claude Code project config; this negation counters
# that one specifically (the .claude/* block further down needs its own separate negation -
# see the comment there). settings.local.json stays ignored: it's per-machine (absolute
# paths, personal permission grants).
!.claude/settings.json

*.trx

TestResults/

_scratchbuild/
_scratchbuild_*/
lmstudio_logs/
ModelTestingResults/
PlanStepRunner/

# Per-run model-eval / research writeups (see docs/research/testing/README.md).
# Untracked by design: new run records accrete continuously and should not require a commit.
/docs/research/

# NOTE: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is itself excluded - a bare
# ".claude/" pattern here would make every !.claude/... negation below a no-op for anything
# not already tracked (this bit us once: enforce-dogfood.ps1 only appeared trackable because
# it was already committed, not because its negation actually worked for new files). So this
# excludes .claude/'s contents file-by-file instead of the directory itself, leaving room for
# the hooks/ and settings.json negations below to actually apply.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**
docs/known-build-warnings.Solution.txt
*.tmp
/.scratch
